From: =?UTF-8?q?Franti=C5=A1ek=20Bal=C3=A1zsy?= <frantisekbalazsy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:25:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: pmp-report: IRQ-safe entries
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A PMP device-state entry that parents PMGR power states (which are IRQ
safe) must be IRQ safe too, or genpd refuses the subdomain. Setting the
state takes a spinlock and polls the acknowledgment atomically, so the
entry may run with interrupts disabled. Opt in with apple,irq-safe.

Tested on a MacBook Pro M4 Pro (J616s): the DISPEXT0 and DISPEXT1
device-state entries parent the dispext0/1 PMGR chains that power the
HDMI and USB-C DisplayPort controllers.

Signed-off-by: František Balázsy <frantisekbalazsy@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
index b650c55707..4b3ce3c656 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
@@ -1556,6 +1556,13 @@ static int apple_pmp_report_entry_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	ent->genpd.power_on = apple_pmp_report_entry_power_on;
 	ent->genpd.power_off = apple_pmp_report_entry_power_off;
+	/*
+	 * An entry that is the parent of PMGR power states (which are IRQ safe)
+	 * must be IRQ safe too. Setting the state takes a spinlock and polls
+	 * the acknowledgment atomically, so it may be called with IRQs off.
+	 */
+	if (of_property_read_bool(node, "apple,irq-safe"))
+		ent->genpd.flags |= GENPD_FLAG_IRQ_SAFE;
 
 	ret = pm_genpd_init(&ent->genpd, NULL, true);
 	if (ret) {
